<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of La Lys (1918)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Battle of the Lys (1918) · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of La Lys was the opening of the German spring offensive in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> known as Operation Georgette, launched on 9 April 1918. The attack fell on the 2nd Portuguese Division holding the line near the Lys river, which was overwhelmed with the loss of over 7,000 men killed, wounded and captured. It was the heaviest defeat of the Portuguese army in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> and is remembered in Portugal as a national tragedy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-la-lys-1918.jpg" alt="Battle of La Lys (1918)" width="320" height="491" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Military Academy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_German_Lys_offensive_1918.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
